{"nodes": [{"id": "packages_docs_docs_guides_character_sets_encodingmapping", "label": "encodingMapping (DICOM term to TextDecoder label)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/docs/docs/guides/character-sets.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_docs_docs_guides_character_sets_normalize_on_read", "label": "ISO_IR 192 Normalize-on-Read", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/docs/docs/guides/character-sets.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "dcmjs deliberately rewrites SpecificCharacterSet to [\"ISO_IR 192\"] on read (keeping the original in _rawValue) and encodes strings as UTF-8 on write, so application code only ever sees JavaScript strings and the output file is self-consistent. Whether to keep this quirk versus surfacing the original charset is an open 1.0 API decision."}, {"id": "packages_docs_docs_guides_character_sets_per_item_contexts", "label": "Per-Sequence-Item Charset Contexts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/docs/docs/guides/character-sets.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_docs_docs_guides_character_sets_charset_passthrough_gate", "label": "charsetPassthroughSafe Gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/docs/docs/guides/character-sets.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Passthrough is only safe when the writer's UTF-8 normalization is byte-stable against the source: absent/empty/ASCII/UTF-8 top-level charsets only. Deliberately conservative \u2014 ISO_IR 100 (Latin-1) sources always re-encode today; a per-element ASCII fast path to widen the gate is planned 1.x work."}], "edges": [{"source": "packages_docs_docs_guides_character_sets_normalize_on_read",